# The linked ScalaScript jar must reach sbt's artifacts, so publishLocal/publish carry it.
# Wiring it as a CLASSIFIED artifact rather than replacing packageBin is deliberate: the plain jar
# holds the Scala facades sscGenerateFacade emits and sbt compiles, so replacing it would publish a
# library missing them. This asserts the classified jar exists; it never touches a remote repo.
> publishLocal
> checkSscArtifact
